{% extends "specification_user.jinja2" %}
{% block requirements %}
Create the Batch Function Specification in English. Use job identifiers such as BAT-001, preferring existing source identifiers. Reference identifiers from the preceding API and data specifications.

## Batch Inventory and Triggers
List job IDs, names, purposes, executing actors, schedules or events, time zones, manual execution, predecessor and successor jobs, and prerequisites.
## Processing by Job
Define arguments, inputs and extraction conditions, processing order, aggregation and transformation, update targets, outputs, and successful completion conditions. Identify related APIs and data fields.
## Operations and Recovery
Describe concurrent launches and mutual exclusion, processing and commit units, idempotency, reruns, retries, resumption, timeouts, rollback and compensation on failure, notifications, logging, and monitoring based on the source.
## Acceptance Criteria
State source-required conditions and expected results for success, no input, partial failure, reruns, and other supported scenarios.
## Consistency and Open Questions
If the source does not describe batch processing, state "Needs confirmation: whether batch processing is required and its scope" without inventing functions. Use Out of scope only when the source explicitly says it is unnecessary, and cite the evidence.
Identify unresolved operational conditions such as schedules and thresholds.
{% endblock %}
